	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="58.1" level="1">Taxation</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="II" level="2">Taxes Administered by Other Agencies</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="26" level="3">Taxation of Public Service Corporations</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="1" level="4">General Provisions</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>58.1-2612</section_number>
	<catch_line>Lien of taxes</catch_line>
	<text>
		All the taxes and levies provided for in this chapter shall, until paid, be a lien upon the property within the Commonwealth of the corporation owning the same and take precedence over all other liens or encumbrances.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, §§ 58-536, 58-599, 58-615; 1984, c. 675.</history>
</law>
